    "description": "<table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:2em; border:2px solid #999; font-size:105%; text-align:center; background:#00008B;\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <td><i><b>This <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Homebrew_Content\" title=\"Homebrew Content\">Homebrew Content</a> has been <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Tested\" title=\"Category:Tested\">Tested</a> per the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Untested\" title=\"Category:Untested\">Untested</a> guidelines. Whether or not it can be used is, as always, the prerogative of the Gamemaster.</b></i> </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p><i>Night Vision Device equipment data created by unknown Wikia user.</i> </p><p>A Night Vision Device grants Darkvision to its users, much like a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Helmet_Package\" title=\"Helmet Package\">Helmet Package</a> grants Low-Light Vision. Installing the Night Vision Device to a helmet or other headwear takes 1 hour, and a DC 20 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Mechanics\" title=\"Mechanics\">Mechanics</a> check. </p><p>When installed in the helmet of a suit of armor (or worn on its own, just as <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Helmet_Package\" title=\"Helmet Package\">Helmet Package</a> can be worn, or installed into other suit type, such as <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Flight_Suit\" title=\"Flight Suit\">Flight Suit</a>), this electronic package allows to grant the wearer ability to ignore <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Concealment\" title=\"Concealment\">Concealment</a> (including <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Total_Concealment\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Total Concealment\">Total Concealment</a>) from darkness, and freely see in and through it unobstructed. It is compatible with a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Helmet_Package\" title=\"Helmet Package\">Helmet Package</a> and other <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Detection_and_Surveillance_Devices\" title=\"Detection and Surveillance Devices\">Detection and Surveillance Devices</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_and_Armor_Accessories\" title=\"Weapon and Armor Accessories\">Weapon and Armor Accessories</a>. </p>",
